From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
Date: Thu, 11 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: monaco-evk: hold refgen on, usb_1 dual-role

usb_2_hsphy takes its PLL supply from refgen, and qcom_snps_hsphy_exit()
disables the PHY's regulators, so the rail goes away every time the PHY is torn
down. Hold refgen on. monaco-monza-som.dtsi already carries the identical
override; upstream added it there as the "REFGEN always-on workaround for USB2
HS PHY" (commit 5238f4e7169f).

usb_1 becomes otg so dwc3 registers a userspace-controllable role switch rather
than coming up peripheral-only. With no role-switch-default-mode the starting
role is still peripheral (drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c), so the PC link is unchanged
until userspace writes "host" to the switch.

Signed-off-by: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet submitted; the refgen hunk mirrors monaco-monza-som.dtsi]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-evk-common.dtsi | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-evk-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-evk-common.dtsi
@@ -666,6 +666,13 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* HW/FW issue prevents REFGEN hardware voting for the USB2 HS PHY, so the PHY
+ * would drop it on exit once a driver is bound. Hold it on, as the Monza SOM does.
+ */
+&refgen {
+	regulator-always-on;
+};
+
 &remoteproc_adsp {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/qcs8300/adsp.mbn";
 
@@ -867,7 +874,7 @@
 };
 
 &usb_1 {
-	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	dr_mode = "otg";
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
